# What EAS Build uploads — this file REPLACES .gitignore for that upload.
#
# It exists for exactly one reason: google-services.json is gitignored,
# because this repo is public and Firebase config, while documented by Google
# as non-secret, is not something to publish by reflex. But the Android build
# genuinely needs it — without it the app cannot register with FCM and
# getExpoPushTokenAsync() has nothing to return, so push registration fails on
# device with a confusing native error.
#
# EAS uses .easignore in preference to .gitignore when it is present, so the
# file below is a copy of .gitignore MINUS the google-services.json line. That
# is the whole trick: the config reaches the builder without ever reaching
# GitHub.
#
# KEEP IN SYNC WITH .gitignore. Because this file shadows it completely, a new
# .gitignore entry added here-but-not-there gets silently uploaded to EAS. The
# expensive mistake would be adding a secret to .gitignore, assuming it is
# excluded everywhere, and shipping it in a build context.

# dependencies
node_modules/

# Expo
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
expo-env.d.ts

# Native
.kotlin/
*.orig.*
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision

# Metro
.metro-health-check*

# debug
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*

# macOS
.DS_Store
*.pem

# local env files
.env*.local

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo

# generated native folders
/ios
/android

# Downloaded Expo Go client (208MB) — never commit
Expo-Go-*.apk
*.apk

# NOTE: google-services.json is deliberately absent from this list. See above.
